  "steps": [
    "Rinse 100g dry sabudana 2 to 3 times, soak in enough water for 4 to 6 hours until soft, then drain thoroughly in a strainer for 10 to 15 minutes.",
    "Steam, peel and mash the sweet potato. Mix with the soaked sabudana, crumbled paneer, green chilli, crushed peanuts, sesame seeds, cumin powder, red chilli powder, sendha namak and coriander.",
    "Mash everything together and shape into 6 equal tikkis.",
    "Lightly brush with oil and air fry at 180°C for 20 minutes, flipping halfway, until golden and crispy.",
    "Blend the peanuts, coriander, mint, green chilli, Greek yogurt and sendha namak to make the green chutney.",
    "Serve the hot and crispy sabudana tikkis with the green yogurt chutney."
  ],
